entry_presets, on the extracted code.

Charon cannot take an inherent method as an entry point, so the crate root
carries a free function per method and those are the names the manifest counts.
A wrapper that quietly did something other than call through would make every
theorem about the method a statement about code nobody runs, so each one is
proven to be its method below.

These are generated by tools/extraction/mirror_crate.py and are the floor, not
the point. The properties that matter go beneath them, and the shapes most of
them take are stated once in NonosExtraction.Shapes.
-/

import NonosExtraction.ArchX8664GdtEntryPresets

open Aeneas Aeneas.Std Result
open nonos_x_arch_x86_64_gdt_entry_presets

set_option linter.hashCommand false
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

namespace NonosExtraction.ArchX8664GdtEntryPresets

/-! ### The forwarding functions add nothing -/

theorem the_gdtentry_kernel_code_64_wrapper_is_its_method :
    gdtentry_kernel_code_64 = arch.x86_64.gdt.entry_presets.GdtEntry.kernel_code_64 := rfl

theorem the_gdtentry_kernel_data_wrapper_is_its_method :
    gdtentry_kernel_data = arch.x86_64.gdt.entry_presets.GdtEntry.kernel_data := rfl

theorem the_gdtentry_user_code_64_wrapper_is_its_method :
    gdtentry_user_code_64 = arch.x86_64.gdt.entry_presets.GdtEntry.user_code_64 := rfl

theorem the_gdtentry_user_data_wrapper_is_its_method :
    gdtentry_user_data = arch.x86_64.gdt.entry_presets.GdtEntry.user_data := rfl

/-! ### Axiom profile -/

#print axioms NonosExtraction.ArchX8664GdtEntryPresets.the_gdtentry_kernel_code_64_wrapper_is_its_method
#print axioms NonosExtraction.ArchX8664GdtEntryPresets.the_gdtentry_kernel_data_wrapper_is_its_method
#print axioms NonosExtraction.ArchX8664GdtEntryPresets.the_gdtentry_user_code_64_wrapper_is_its_method
#print axioms NonosExtraction.ArchX8664GdtEntryPresets.the_gdtentry_user_data_wrapper_is_its_method

end NonosExtraction.ArchX8664GdtEntryPresets
